   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECR302 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.3</span>\n<h2>The 10 course learning outcomes (CLO), verbatim</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Exam questions are written against these outcomes — use them as your checklist.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 14238 (subject ECR301, used as reference) · Decision 444/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 23/04/2026 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECR302 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.3</span>\n<h2>10 chuẩn đầu ra môn học (CLO), nguyên văn</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Đề thi được ra theo các chuẩn đầu ra này — dùng chúng làm danh sách tự kiểm.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 14238 (môn ECR301, dùng làm tham khảo) · QĐ 444/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 23/04/2026 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>CLO</th><th>Details (verbatim)<br><small>Nội dung (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td><strong>CLO1</strong></td><td>Apply appropriate reading strategies (skimming, scanning, close reading, analytical reading) to different text types and demonstrate critical reading skills by creating annotated texts that identify assumptions, evaluate evidence, and question arguments (using Claude, NotebookLM for analysis verification and pattern recognition)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>CLO2</strong></td><td>Evaluate the academic credibility of texts by analyzing peer-review status, publication sources, and currency, and create a comparative analysis demonstrating why peer-reviewed sources are preferable for academic research (using using AI-powered fact-checkers and source analyzers: Turnitin, Semantic Scholar AI)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td><strong>CLO3</strong></td><td>Analyze author credibility and potential bias by examining author background, funding sources, and quoted authorities, and produce a bias assessment report with specific examples and reasoning (using AI bias detection tools: Claude, Perspective API, Media Bias/Fact Check AI)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td><strong>CLO4</strong></td><td>Identify and assess author stance, intended audience, and purpose by analyzing rhetorical choices, tone, and context, and present findings through structured analysis templates (using sentiment analysis and rhetorical analysis AI: ChatGPT, Grammarly Tone Detector, Claude)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td><strong>CLO5</strong></td><td>Distinguish between factual claims and opinions by categorizing statements and construct evidence-based arguments that clearly separate verifiable facts from subjective interpretations (using AI classification tools: Google Fact Check Tools)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td><strong>CLO6</strong></td><td>Evaluate empirical research reports by applying scientific method criteria and create structured reviews that assess methodology, data quality, and conclusion validity (using AI research analysis platforms: Semantic Scholar)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td><strong>CLO7</strong></td><td>Assess the strength and reliability of different evidence types (anecdotal, statistical, visual, testimonial) and design evidence evaluation frameworks for various persuasive techniques (using AI-powered statistical analysis tools: Tableau Public, ChatGPT for stats - Stats.ai)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td><strong>CLO8</strong></td><td>Contextualize texts within broader intellectual frameworks by identifying schools of thought and compare how different theoretical perspectives influence interpretation and analysis (Using AI knowledge graphs and contextual analysis tools: NotebookLM, Claude, Connected Papers)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td><strong>CLO9</strong></td><td>Analyze the relationship between personal experience and textual interpretation and develop strategies for maintaining objectivity while acknowledging subjective responses (using AI reflection prompts and bias-checking tools: Claude, Perspective API)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td><strong>CLO10</strong></td><td>Synthesize critical review components (summary, analysis, evaluation) to produce well-structured critical reviews that demonstrate comprehensive analytical thinking (using AI writing assistants and structure analyzers: ChatGPT, Grammarly, Hemingway Editor)</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14238\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14238</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14238\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14238</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
